; pictures' formats decoded, the two born of the web: WebP (Webp: the
; container; Vp8l: the lossless format; Vp8: the lossy one, a frame of
; the VP8 video codec) and SVG (Svg: a drawing read and made pixels;
; elm-playground's, copied to be told here and to grow). The older
; formats (GIF, PNG, JPEG) came to the web from outside and stay
; elm-playground's. Pure OCaml, bytes in and pixels out.
(library
 (name mini_images)
 (wrapped false)
 (libraries
   tiny_libs.graphics_rgba ; Rgba_image: the pixels given back
   mini_dom lang_xml ; Dom, Xml: a drawing is a document, an SVG file read
   tiny_libs.compression ; Huffman: the lossless format's prefix codes
   ; Svg's: polygons filled and stroked (Fill, Stroke, Framebuffer),
   ; curves made lines and transforms composed (Curve, Affine)
   tiny_libs.graphics_core tiny_libs.graphics_2d tiny_libs.graphics_2d_geometry))
